ib37","tag":"li","text":"Muandet et al. [2020] Krikamol Muandet, Arash Mehrjou, Si Kai Lee, and Anant Raj. Dual instrumental variable regression. Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems , 2020."},{"child_ids":["bib.bib38.1"],"classes":["ltx_bibitem"],"id":"bib.bib38","tag":"li","text":"Della Vecchia and Basu [2023] Riccardo Della Vecchia and Debabrota Basu. Stochastic online instrumental variable regression: Regrets for endogeneity and bandit feedback. arXiv e-prints , pages arXiv–2302, 2023."},{"child_ids":[],"classes":["ltx_bibitem"],"id":"bib.bib39","tag":"li","text":"Chen et al. [2024] Xuxing Chen, Abhishek Roy, Yifan Hu, and Krishnakumar Balasubramanian. Stochastic optimization algorithms for instrumental variable regression with streaming data, 2024. URL https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.19463 ."},{"child_ids":["bib.bib40.1"],"classes":["ltx_bibitem"],"id":"bib.bib40","tag":"li","text":"Peixoto et al. [2024] Caio Peixoto, Yuri Saporito, and Yuri Fonseca. Nonparametric instrumental variable regression through stochastic approximate gradients. arXiv preprint arXiv:2402.05639 , 2024."},{"child_ids":["bib.bib41.1"],"classes":["ltx_bibitem"],"id":"bib.bib41","tag":"li","text":"Stock and Watson [2011] J.H. Stock and M.W. Watson. Introduction to Econometrics . Addison-Wesley series in economics. Addison-Wesley, 2011. ISBN 9780138009007. URL https://books.google.com/books?id=prLxRQAACAAJ ."},{"child_ids":[],"classes":["ltx_bibitem"],"id":"bib.bib42","tag":"li","text":"Tropp [2015] Joel A. Tropp. An introduction to matrix concentration inequalities, 2015. URL https://arxiv.org/abs/1501.01571 ."},{"child_ids":[],"classes":["ltx_bibitem"],"id":"bib.bib43","tag":"li","text":"Jin et al. [2024] Yanhao Jin, Krishnakumar Balasubramanian, and Debashis Paul. Meta-learning with generalized ridge regression: High-dimensional asymptotics, optimality and hyper-covariance estimation, 2024."},{"child_ids":[],"classes":["ltx_bibitem"],"id":"bib.bib44","tag":"li","text":"Rudelson and Vershynin [2010] Mark Rudelson and Roman Vershynin. Non-asymptotic theory of random matrices: extreme singular values, 2010. URL https://arxiv.org/abs/1003.2990 ."},{"child_ids":["A1.SS1.p1.1"],"classes":["ltx_para","ltx_noindent"],"id":"A1.SS1.p1","tag":"div","text":"We first introduce the following lemmas that are used in the proof of Theorem 2.1 ."},{"child_ids":["A1.Ex8"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx28","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle\\mathbb{E}[\\boldsymbol{S}_{i}]=\\boldsymbol{0},\\mathbb{P}(\\left\\|\\boldsymbol{S}_{i}\\right\\|\\leq b)=1,\\quad\\forall i=1,\\ldots,n.$"},{"child_ids":["A1.Ex9"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx29","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}=\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\boldsymbol{S}_{i},$"},{"child_ids":["A1.Ex10"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx30","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle\\nu(\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}):=\\max\\{\\left\\|\\mathbb{E}(\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}^{\\top})\\right\\|,\\left\\|\\mathbb{E}(\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega})\\right\\|\\},$"},{"child_ids":["A1.Ex11"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx31","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle\\mathbb{P}\\{\\left\\|\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\}\\leq(d_{1}+d_{2})\\cdot\\exp\\left(\\frac{-\\varepsilon^{2}/2}{\\nu(\\boldsymbol{\\Omega})+b\\varepsilon/3}\\right)\\text{ for any }\\varepsilon\\geq 0.$"},{"child_ids":["A1.Thmlemma1.p1.1","A1.EGx28","A1.Ex8","A1.Thmlemma1.p1.2","A1.EGx29","A1.Ex9","A1.Thmlemma1.p1.3","A1.EGx30","A1.Ex10","A1.Thmlemma1.p1.4","A1.EGx31","A1.Ex11"],"classes":["ltx_para"],"id":"A1.Thmlemma1.p1","tag":"div","text":"Let $\\boldsymbol{S}_{1},\\ldots,\\boldsymbol{S}_{n}$ be independent, centered random matrices with common dimension $d_{1}\\times d_{2}$ , and assume that each one is almost surely bounded: $\\displaystyle\\mathbb{E}[\\boldsymbol{S}_{i}]=\\boldsymbol{0},\\mathbb{P}(\\left\\|\\boldsymbol{S}_{i}\\right\\|\\leq b)=1,\\quad\\forall i=1,\\ldots,n.$ With the sum: $\\displaystyle\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}=\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\boldsymbol{S}_{i},$ and the matrix variance statistic of the sum: $\\displaystyle\\nu(\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}):=\\max\\{\\left\\|\\mathbb{E}(\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}^{\\top})\\right\\|,\\left\\|\\mathbb{E}(\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega})\\right\\|\\},$ then the following inequality holds: $\\displaystyle\\mathbb{P}\\{\\left\\|\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\}\\leq(d_{1}+d_{2})\\cdot\\exp\\left(\\frac{-\\varepsilon^{2}/2}{\\nu(\\boldsymbol{\\Omega})+b\\varepsilon/3}\\right)\\text{ for any }\\varepsilon\\geq 0.$"},{"child_ids":["A1.Thmlemma1.2","A1.Thmlemma1.3","A1.Thmlemma1.4","A1.Thmlemma1.p1","A1.Thmlemma1.p1.1","A1.EGx28","A1.Ex8","A1.Thmlemma1.p1.2","A1.EGx29","A1.Ex9","A1.Thmlemma1.p1.3","A1.EGx30","A1.Ex10","A1.Thmlemma1.p1.4","A1.EGx31","A1.Ex11"],"classes":["ltx_theorem","ltx_theorem_lemma"],"id":"A1.Thmlemma1","tag":"div","text":"Lemma A.1 (Bernstein Inequality, from Theorem 6.1.1 in Tropp [2015] ). Let $\\boldsymbol{S}_{1},\\ldots,\\boldsymbol{S}_{n}$ be independent, centered random matrices with common dimension $d_{1}\\times d_{2}$ , and assume that each one is almost surely bounded: $\\displaystyle\\mathbb{E}[\\boldsymbol{S}_{i}]=\\boldsymbol{0},\\mathbb{P}(\\left\\|\\boldsymbol{S}_{i}\\right\\|\\leq b)=1,\\quad\\forall i=1,\\ldots,n.$ With the sum: $\\displaystyle\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}=\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\boldsymbol{S}_{i},$ and the matrix variance statistic of the sum: $\\displaystyle\\nu(\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}):=\\max\\{\\left\\|\\mathbb{E}(\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}^{\\top})\\right\\|,\\left\\|\\mathbb{E}(\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega})\\right\\|\\},$ then the following inequality holds: $\\displaystyle\\mathbb{P}\\{\\left\\|\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\}\\leq(d_{1}+d_{2})\\cdot\\exp\\left(\\frac{-\\varepsilon^{2}/2}{\\nu(\\boldsymbol{\\Omega})+b\\varepsilon/3}\\right)\\text{ for any }\\varepsilon\\geq 0.$"},{"child_ids":["A1.Ex12"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx32","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle(\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)})^{-1}\\overset{\\textsf{p}}{\\rightarrow}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}^{-1}.$"},{"child_ids":["A1.Ex13"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx33","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\leq\\xi(n,\\varepsilon),$"},{"child_ids":["A1.Ex14"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx34","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|(\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)})^{-1}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}^{-1}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\leq\\xi(n,\\tilde{\\lambda}^{2}\\varepsilon).$"},{"child_ids":["A1.Thmlemma2.p1.1","A1.EGx32","A1.Ex12","A1.Thmlemma2.p1.2","A1.EGx33","A1.Ex13","A1.Thmlemma2.p1.3","A1.EGx34","A1.Ex14"],"classes":["ltx_para"],"id":"A1.Thmlemma2.p1","tag":"div","text":"Suppose we have a random invertible matrix $\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}$ and invertible matrix sequence $\\{\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)}\\}$ such that $\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)}\\overset{\\textsf{p}}{\\rightarrow}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}$ . If there exists a constant $\\tilde{\\lambda}>0$ such that $\\sigma_{\\min}(\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}})\\geq\\tilde{\\lambda}$ almost surely, then it holds that: $\\displaystyle(\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)})^{-1}\\overset{\\textsf{p}}{\\rightarrow}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}^{-1}.$ Further, given convergence rate $\\displaystyle\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\leq\\xi(n,\\varepsilon),$ then: $\\displaystyle\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|(\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)})^{-1}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}^{-1}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\leq\\xi(n,\\tilde{\\lambda}^{2}\\varepsilon).$"},{"child_ids":["A1.Thmlemma2.2","A1.Thmlemma2.3","A1.Thmlemma2.4","A1.Thmlemma2.p1","A1.Thmlemma2.p1.1","A1.EGx32","A1.Ex12","A1.Thmlemma2.p1.2","A1.EGx33","A1.Ex13","A1.Thmlemma2.p1.3","A1.EGx34","A1.Ex14"],"classes":["ltx_theorem","ltx_theorem_lemma"],"id":"A1.Thmlemma2","tag":"div","text":"Lemma A.2 (Inverse Convergence, adapted from Lemma 2.1 in Jin et al. [2024] ). Suppose we have a random invertible matrix $\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}$ and invertible matrix sequence $\\{\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)}\\}$ such that $\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)}\\overset{\\textsf{p}}{\\rightarrow}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}$ . If there exists a constant $\\tilde{\\lambda}>0$ such that $\\sigma_{\\min}(\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}})\\geq\\tilde{\\lambda}$ almost surely, then it holds that: $\\displaystyle(\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)})^{-1}\\overset{\\textsf{p}}{\\rightarrow}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}^{-1}.$ Further, given convergence rate $\\displaystyle\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\leq\\xi(n,\\varepsilon),$ then: $\\displaystyle\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|(\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)})^{-1}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}^{-1}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\leq\\xi(n,\\tilde{\\lambda}^{2}\\varepsilon).$"},{"child_ids":["A1.Ex15"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx35","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle(\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)})^{-1}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}^{-1}=(\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)})^{-1}(\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}-\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)})\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}^{-1}.$"},{"child_ids":["A1.Ex16","A1.Ex17"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx36","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle\\left\\|(\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)})^{-1}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}^{-1}\\right\\|$ $\\displaystyle\\leq\\left\\|(\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)})^{-1}\\right\\|\\left\\|\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}-\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)}\\right\\|\\left\\|\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}^{-1}\\right\\|$ $\\displaystyle\\leq\\frac{1}{\\tilde{\\lambda}^{2}}\\left\\|\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}-\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)}\\right\\|.$"},{"child_ids":["A1.Ex18"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx37","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle\\begin{split}\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|(\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)})^{-1}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}^{-1}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}&\\leq\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\frac{1}{\\tilde{\\lambda}^{2}}\\left\\|\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}-\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\\\ &\\leq\\xi(n,\\tilde{\\lambda}^{2}\\varepsilon).\\end{split}$"},{"child_ids":["A1.SS1.p2.1","A1.SS1.p2.1.1","A1.EGx35","A1.Ex15","A1.SS1.p2.2","A1.SS1.p2.2.1","A1.EGx36","A1.Ex16","A1.Ex17","A1.SS1.p2.3","A1.SS1.p2.3.1","A1.EGx37","A1.Ex18","A1.SS1.p2.4","A1.SS1.p2.4.1"],"classes":["ltx_para"],"id":"A1.SS1.p2","tag":"div","text":"We have the following decomposition: $\\displaystyle(\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)})^{-1}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}^{-1}=(\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)})^{-1}(\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}-\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)})\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}^{-1}.$ It follows that: $\\displaystyle\\left\\|(\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)})^{-1}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}^{-1}\\right\\|$ $\\displaystyle\\leq\\left\\|(\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)})^{-1}\\right\\|\\left\\|\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}-\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)}\\right\\|\\left\\|\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}^{-1}\\right\\|$ $\\displaystyle\\leq\\frac{1}{\\tilde{\\lambda}^{2}}\\left\\|\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}-\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)}\\right\\|.$ Then $\\displaystyle\\begin{split}\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|(\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)})^{-1}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}^{-1}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}&\\leq\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\frac{1}{\\tilde{\\lambda}^{2}}\\left\\|\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}-\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}^{(n)}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\\\ &\\leq\\xi(n,\\tilde{\\lambda}^{2}\\varepsilon).\\end{split}$ ∎"},{"child_ids":["A1.Ex19"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx38","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\cdots\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}\\overset{\\textsf{p}}{\\rightarrow}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\cdots\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K}.$"},{"child_ids":["A1.Thmlemma3.p1.1","A1.EGx38","A1.Ex19"],"classes":["ltx_para","ltx_noindent"],"id":"A1.Thmlemma3.p1","tag":"div","text":"Let $\\{\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\},\\{\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\},\\ldots,\\{\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}\\}$ be $K$ sequences of matrices such that $\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\overset{\\textsf{p}}{\\rightarrow}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}$ , $\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\overset{\\textsf{p}}{\\rightarrow}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2},\\ldots,\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}\\overset{\\textsf{p}}{\\rightarrow}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K}$ , where each $\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{k}^{(n)}\\|$ is almost surely bounded for every $k=1,\\ldots,K$ . If the dimensions match, then it holds that: $\\displaystyle\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\cdots\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}\\overset{\\textsf{p}}{\\rightarrow}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\cdots\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K}.$"},{"child_ids":["A1.Ex20"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx39","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle\\begin{split}\\mathbb{P}&\\left\\{\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\leq\\xi_{1}(n,\\varepsilon),\\\\ \\mathbb{P}&\\left\\{\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\leq\\xi_{2}(n,\\varepsilon),\\\\ &\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\vdots\\\\ \\mathbb{P}&\\left\\{\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\leq\\xi_{K}(n,\\varepsilon),\\end{split}$"},{"child_ids":["A1.E15"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx40","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\cdots\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\cdots\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}$ $\\displaystyle\\leq\\sum_{i=1}^{K}\\xi_{i}\\left(n,\\frac{\\varepsilon}{K\\prod_{k\\neq i}^{K}M_{k}}\\right),$ (15)"},{"child_ids":["A1.Thmlemma3.p2.1","A1.EGx39","A1.Ex20","A1.Thmlemma3.p2.2","A1.EGx40","A1.E15","A1.Thmlemma3.p2.3"],"classes":["ltx_para"],"id":"A1.Thmlemma3.p2","tag":"div","text":"Further, given convergence rates: $\\displaystyle\\begin{split}\\mathbb{P}&\\left\\{\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\leq\\xi_{1}(n,\\varepsilon),\\\\ \\mathbb{P}&\\left\\{\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\leq\\xi_{2}(n,\\varepsilon),\\\\ &\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\vdots\\\\ \\mathbb{P}&\\left\\{\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\leq\\xi_{K}(n,\\varepsilon),\\end{split}$ then it holds that: $\\displaystyle\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\cdots\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\cdots\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}$ $\\displaystyle\\leq\\sum_{i=1}^{K}\\xi_{i}\\left(n,\\frac{\\varepsilon}{K\\prod_{k\\neq i}^{K}M_{k}}\\right),$ (15) where $M_{k}$ is an upper bound such that $\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{k}^{(n)}\\|\\leq M_{k}$ almost surely, $\\forall k=1,\\ldots,K$ ."},{"child_ids":["A1.Thmlemma3.2","A1.Thmlemma3.3","A1.Thmlemma3.4","A1.Thmlemma3.p1","A1.Thmlemma3.p1.1","A1.EGx38","A1.Ex19","A1.Thmlemma3.p2","A1.Thmlemma3.p2.1","A1.EGx39","A1.Ex20","A1.Thmlemma3.p2.2","A1.EGx40","A1.E15","A1.Thmlemma3.p2.3"],"classes":["ltx_theorem","ltx_theorem_lemma"],"id":"A1.Thmlemma3","tag":"div","text":"Lemma A.3 (Product Convergence). Let $\\{\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\},\\{\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\},\\ldots,\\{\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}\\}$ be $K$ sequences of matrices such that $\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\overset{\\textsf{p}}{\\rightarrow}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}$ , $\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\overset{\\textsf{p}}{\\rightarrow}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2},\\ldots,\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}\\overset{\\textsf{p}}{\\rightarrow}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K}$ , where each $\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{k}^{(n)}\\|$ is almost surely bounded for every $k=1,\\ldots,K$ . If the dimensions match, then it holds that: $\\displaystyle\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\cdots\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}\\overset{\\textsf{p}}{\\rightarrow}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\cdots\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K}.$ Further, given convergence rates: $\\displaystyle\\begin{split}\\mathbb{P}&\\left\\{\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\leq\\xi_{1}(n,\\varepsilon),\\\\ \\mathbb{P}&\\left\\{\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\leq\\xi_{2}(n,\\varepsilon),\\\\ &\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\vdots\\\\ \\mathbb{P}&\\left\\{\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\leq\\xi_{K}(n,\\varepsilon),\\end{split}$ then it holds that: $\\displaystyle\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\cdots\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\cdots\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}$ $\\displaystyle\\leq\\sum_{i=1}^{K}\\xi_{i}\\left(n,\\frac{\\varepsilon}{K\\prod_{k\\neq i}^{K}M_{k}}\\right),$ (15) where $M_{k}$ is an upper bound such that $\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{k}^{(n)}\\|\\leq M_{k}$ almost surely, $\\forall k=1,\\ldots,K$ ."},{"child_ids":["A1.Ex21"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx41","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle\\begin{aligned} \\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\right\\|&\\leq\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\right\\|+\\left\\|\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\right\\|\\\\ &\\leq\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\right\\|\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\right\\|+\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\right\\|\\left\\|\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\right\\|\\\\ &\\leq M_{2}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\right\\|+M_{1}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\right\\|.\\end{aligned}$"},{"child_ids":["A1.Ex22"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx42","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle\\begin{split}&\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\\\ \\leq&\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{M_{2}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\right\\|+M_{1}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\\\ \\leq&\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{M_{2}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon/2\\right\\}+\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{M_{1}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon/2\\right\\}\\\\ \\leq&\\xi_{1}\\left(n,\\frac{\\varepsilon}{2M_{2}}\\right)+\\xi_{2}\\left(n,\\frac{\\varepsilon}{2M_{1}}\\right).\\end{split}$"},{"child_ids":["A1.E16"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx43","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle\\begin{split}&\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\cdots\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\cdots\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K}\\right\\|\\\\ &\\leq\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\cdots\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\cdots\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K-1}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}\\right\\|+\\left\\|\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\cdots\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K-1}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\cdots\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K}\\right\\|\\\\ &\\leq M_{K}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\cdots\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K-1}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\cdots\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K-1}\\right\\|+\\prod_{k=1}^{K-1}M_{k}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K}\\right\\|.\\\\ \\end{split}$ (16)"},{"child_ids":["A1.Ex23"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx44","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle\\begin{split}&\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\cdots\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\cdots\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\\\ &\\leq\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{M_{K}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\cdots\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K-1}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\cdots\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K-1}\\right\\|+\\prod_{k=1}^{K-1}M_{k}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\\\ &\\leq\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{M_{K}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\cdots\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K-1}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\cdots\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K-1}\\right\\|\\geq\\frac{K-1}{K}\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\\\ &\\qquad+\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\prod_{k=1}^{K-1}M_{k}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K}\\right\\|\\geq\\frac{1}{K}\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\\\ &\\leq\\sum_{i=1}^{K-1}\\xi_{i}\\left(n,\\frac{\\varepsilon}{KM_{K}\\prod_{k\\neq i}^{K-1}M_{k}}\\right)+\\xi_{K}\\left(n,\\frac{\\varepsilon}{K\\prod_{k=1}^{K-1}M_{k}}\\right)\\\\ &=\\sum_{i=1}^{K}\\xi_{i}\\left(n,\\frac{\\varepsilon}{K\\prod_{k\\neq i}^{K}M_{k}}\\right).\\end{split}$"},{"child_ids":["A1.SS1.p3.1","A1.SS1.p3.1.1","A1.EGx41","A1.Ex21","A1.SS1.p3.2","A1.SS1.p3.2.1","A1.EGx42","A1.Ex22","A1.SS1.p3.3","A1.SS1.p3.3.1","A1.EGx43","A1.E16","A1.SS1.p3.4","A1.SS1.p3.4.1","A1.EGx44","A1.Ex23","A1.SS1.p3.5","A1.SS1.p3.5.1"],"classes":["ltx_para"],"id":"A1.SS1.p3","tag":"div","text":"We begin by showing the case of $K=2$ . By the triangle inequality, we have: $\\displaystyle\\begin{aligned} \\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\right\\|&\\leq\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\right\\|+\\left\\|\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\right\\|\\\\ &\\leq\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\right\\|\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\right\\|+\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\right\\|\\left\\|\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\right\\|\\\\ &\\leq M_{2}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\right\\|+M_{1}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\right\\|.\\end{aligned}$ Using the union bound, we have: $\\displaystyle\\begin{split}&\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\\\ \\leq&\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{M_{2}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\right\\|+M_{1}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\\\ \\leq&\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{M_{2}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon/2\\right\\}+\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{M_{1}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon/2\\right\\}\\\\ \\leq&\\xi_{1}\\left(n,\\frac{\\varepsilon}{2M_{2}}\\right)+\\xi_{2}\\left(n,\\frac{\\varepsilon}{2M_{1}}\\right).\\end{split}$ For any $K>2$ , suppose the statement (15 ) holds for $k=2,\\ldots,K-1$ . Observe that: $\\displaystyle\\begin{split}&\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\cdots\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\cdots\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K}\\right\\|\\\\ &\\leq\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\cdots\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\cdots\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K-1}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}\\right\\|+\\left\\|\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\cdots\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K-1}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\cdots\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K}\\right\\|\\\\ &\\leq M_{K}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\cdots\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K-1}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\cdots\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K-1}\\right\\|+\\prod_{k=1}^{K-1}M_{k}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K}\\right\\|.\\\\ \\end{split}$ (16) Then it follows that: $\\displaystyle\\begin{split}&\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\cdots\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\cdots\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\\\ &\\leq\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{M_{K}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\cdots\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K-1}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\cdots\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K-1}\\right\\|+\\prod_{k=1}^{K-1}M_{k}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\\\ &\\leq\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{M_{K}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\cdots\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K-1}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{2}\\cdots\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K-1}\\right\\|\\geq\\frac{K-1}{K}\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\\\ &\\qquad+\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\prod_{k=1}^{K-1}M_{k}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{K}\\right\\|\\geq\\frac{1}{K}\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\\\ &\\leq\\sum_{i=1}^{K-1}\\xi_{i}\\left(n,\\frac{\\varepsilon}{KM_{K}\\prod_{k\\neq i}^{K-1}M_{k}}\\right)+\\xi_{K}\\left(n,\\frac{\\varepsilon}{K\\prod_{k=1}^{K-1}M_{k}}\\right)\\\\ &=\\sum_{i=1}^{K}\\xi_{i}\\left(n,\\frac{\\varepsilon}{K\\prod_{k\\neq i}^{K}M_{k}}\\right).\\end{split}$ Thus, by induction, the proof is complete. ∎"},{"child_ids":["A1.Ex24"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx45","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle\\begin{split}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\cdots\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{0}\\right\\|&\\leq\\prod_{k=2}^{K}M_{k}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\right\\|.\\end{split}$"},{"child_ids":["A1.Ex25"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx46","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle\\begin{split}\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\cdots\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{0}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}&\\leq\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\prod_{k=2}^{K}M_{k}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\\\ &\\leq\\xi_{1}\\left(n,\\frac{\\varepsilon}{\\prod_{k=2}^{K}M_{k}}\\right).\\end{split}$"},{"child_ids":["A1.Thmrmk1.p1.1","A1.EGx45","A1.Ex24","A1.Thmrmk1.p1.2","A1.EGx46","A1.Ex25"],"classes":["ltx_para"],"id":"A1.Thmrmk1.p1","tag":"div","text":"In Lemma A.3 , consider the special case where $\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}=\\boldsymbol{0}$ . Then the inequality (16 ) can be simplified as follows: $\\displaystyle\\begin{split}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\cdots\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{0}\\right\\|&\\leq\\prod_{k=2}^{K}M_{k}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\right\\|.\\end{split}$ And we have the following simplified form: $\\displaystyle\\begin{split}\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\cdots\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{0}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}&\\leq\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\prod_{k=2}^{K}M_{k}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\\\ &\\leq\\xi_{1}\\left(n,\\frac{\\varepsilon}{\\prod_{k=2}^{K}M_{k}}\\right).\\end{split}$"},{"child_ids":["A1.Thmrmk1.2","A1.Thmrmk1.3","A1.Thmrmk1.p1","A1.Thmrmk1.p1.1","A1.EGx45","A1.Ex24","A1.Thmrmk1.p1.2","A1.EGx46","A1.Ex25"],"classes":["ltx_theorem","ltx_theorem_rmk"],"id":"A1.Thmrmk1","tag":"div","text":"Remark A.1 . In Lemma A.3 , consider the special case where $\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{1}=\\boldsymbol{0}$ . Then the inequality (16 ) can be simplified as follows: $\\displaystyle\\begin{split}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\cdots\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{0}\\right\\|&\\leq\\prod_{k=2}^{K}M_{k}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\right\\|.\\end{split}$ And we have the following simplified form: $\\displaystyle\\begin{split}\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{2}^{(n)}\\cdots\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{K}^{(n)}-\\boldsymbol{0}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}&\\leq\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\prod_{k=2}^{K}M_{k}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{1}^{(n)}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\right\\}\\\\ &\\leq\\xi_{1}\\left(n,\\frac{\\varepsilon}{\\prod_{k=2}^{K}M_{k}}\\right).\\end{split}$"},{"child_ids":["A1.E17"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx47","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle\\begin{split}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\beta}}_{\\textsf{2SLS}}&=\\left(\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Theta}}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Theta}}\\right)^{-1}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Theta}}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Y}\\\\ &=\\left[\\left((\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z})^{-1}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{X}\\right)^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}(\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z})^{-1}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{X}\\right]^{-1}\\left((\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z})^{-1}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{X}\\right)^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Y}\\\\ &=\\left(\\boldsymbol{X}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}(\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z})^{-1}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{X}\\right)^{-1}\\boldsymbol{X}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}(\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z})^{-1}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Y}\\\\ &=\\boldsymbol{\\beta}+\\left(\\boldsymbol{X}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}(\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z})^{-1}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{X}\\right)^{-1}\\boldsymbol{X}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}(\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z})^{-1}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{\\mathcal{E}}_{1}.\\end{split}$ (17)"},{"child_ids":["A1.SS1.p4.1","A1.SS1.p4.1.1","A1.SS1.p4.1.1.1","A1.EGx47","A1.E17","A1.SS1.p4.2","A1.SS1.p4.2.1"],"classes":["ltx_para","ltx_noindent"],"id":"A1.SS1.p4","tag":"div","text":"We denote the observational values $(\\boldsymbol{Z},\\boldsymbol{X},\\boldsymbol{Y})=\\{(\\boldsymbol{z}_{i},\\boldsymbol{x}_{i},y_{i})\\}_{i=1}^{n}$ , and $\\boldsymbol{\\mathcal{E}}_{1}=\\{\\epsilon_{1,i}\\}_{i=1}^{n}$ . The 2SLS estimator is given by: $\\displaystyle\\begin{split}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\beta}}_{\\textsf{2SLS}}&=\\left(\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Theta}}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Theta}}\\right)^{-1}\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Theta}}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Y}\\\\ &=\\left[\\left((\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z})^{-1}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{X}\\right)^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}(\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z})^{-1}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{X}\\right]^{-1}\\left((\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z})^{-1}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{X}\\right)^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Y}\\\\ &=\\left(\\boldsymbol{X}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}(\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z})^{-1}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{X}\\right)^{-1}\\boldsymbol{X}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}(\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z})^{-1}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Y}\\\\ &=\\boldsymbol{\\beta}+\\left(\\boldsymbol{X}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}(\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z})^{-1}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{X}\\right)^{-1}\\boldsymbol{X}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}(\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z})^{-1}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{\\mathcal{E}}_{1}.\\end{split}$ (17) We first consider the case when event $\\mathcal{A}$ is true. Let $\\boldsymbol{Q}_{zz}:=\\mathbb{E}[\\boldsymbol{z}\\boldsymbol{z}^{\\top}|\\mathcal{A}],\\boldsymbol{Q}_{zx}:=\\mathbb{E}[\\boldsymbol{z}\\boldsymbol{x}^{\\top}|\\mathcal{A}]$ , $\\bar{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{zz}:=\\sum_{i=1}^{n}(\\boldsymbol{z}_{i}\\boldsymbol{z}_{i}^{\\top}-\\boldsymbol{Q}_{zz}),\\bar{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{zx}:=\\sum_{i=1}^{n}(\\boldsymbol{z}_{i}\\boldsymbol{x}_{i}^{\\top}-\\boldsymbol{Q}_{zx}),\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{z\\epsilon_{1}}:=\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\boldsymbol{z}_{i}\\epsilon_{1,i}$ ."},{"child_ids":["A1.SS1.p5.1","A1.SS1.p5.1.1"],"classes":["ltx_para","ltx_noindent"],"id":"A1.SS1.p5","tag":"div","text":"Let $\\bar{B}_{zz},\\bar{B}_{zx},B_{zx},B_{z\\epsilon_{1}}$ be some upper bounds such that $\\left\\|\\boldsymbol{z}_{i}\\boldsymbol{z}_{i}^{\\top}-\\boldsymbol{Q}_{zz}\\right\\|\\leq\\bar{B}_{zz},\\left\\|\\boldsymbol{z}_{i}\\boldsymbol{x}_{i}^{\\top}-\\boldsymbol{Q}_{zx}\\right\\|\\leq\\bar{B}_{zx},\\left\\|\\boldsymbol{z}_{i}\\boldsymbol{x}_{i}^{\\top}\\right\\|\\leq B_{zx},\\left\\|\\boldsymbol{z}_{i}\\epsilon_{1,i}\\right\\|\\leq B_{z\\epsilon_{1}}$ almost surely, for all $i=1,\\ldots,n$ . The existence of $\\bar{B}_{zz},\\bar{B}_{zx},B_{zx},B_{z\\epsilon_{1}}$ is guaranteed under Assumption 2 ."},{"child_ids":["A1.E18"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx48","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle\\begin{split}\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\frac{\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}}{n}-\\boldsymbol{Q}_{zz}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\middle|\\mathcal{A}\\right\\}&=\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\boldsymbol{z}_{i}\\boldsymbol{z}_{i}^{\\top}}{n}-\\boldsymbol{Q}_{zz}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\middle|\\mathcal{A}\\right\\}\\\\ &=\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\sum_{i=1}^{n}(\\boldsymbol{z}_{i}\\boldsymbol{z}_{i}^{\\top}-\\boldsymbol{Q}_{zz})\\right\\|\\geq n\\varepsilon\\middle|\\mathcal{A}\\right\\}\\\\ &\\leq 2q\\exp\\left(-\\frac{n^{2}\\varepsilon^{2}/2}{\\nu(\\bar{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{zz}|\\mathcal{A})+\\bar{B}_{zz}n\\varepsilon/3}\\right).\\end{split}$ (18)"},{"child_ids":["A1.E19"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx49","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle\\begin{split}\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\frac{\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{X}}{n}-\\boldsymbol{Q}_{zx}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\middle|\\mathcal{A}\\right\\}&=\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\boldsymbol{z}_{i}\\boldsymbol{x}_{i}^{\\top}}{n}-\\boldsymbol{Q}_{zx}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\middle|\\mathcal{A}\\right\\}\\\\ &=\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\sum_{i=1}^{n}(\\boldsymbol{z}_{i}\\boldsymbol{x}_{i}^{\\top}-\\boldsymbol{Q}_{zx})\\right\\|\\geq n\\varepsilon\\middle|\\mathcal{A}\\right\\}\\\\ &\\leq(p+q)\\exp\\left(-\\frac{n^{2}\\varepsilon^{2}/2}{\\nu(\\bar{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{zx}|\\mathcal{A})+\\bar{B}_{zx}n\\varepsilon/3}\\right).\\end{split}$ (19)"},{"child_ids":["A1.E20"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx50","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle\\begin{split}\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\frac{\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{\\mathcal{E}}_{1}}{n}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\middle|\\mathcal{A}\\right\\}&=\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\boldsymbol{z}_{i}{\\epsilon}_{1,i}}{n}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\middle|\\mathcal{A}\\right\\}\\\\ &=\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\boldsymbol{z}_{i}{\\epsilon}_{1,i}\\right\\|\\geq n\\varepsilon\\middle|\\mathcal{A}\\right\\}\\\\ &\\leq(q+1)\\exp\\left(-\\frac{n^{2}\\varepsilon^{2}/2}{\\nu(\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{z\\epsilon_{1}}|\\mathcal{A})+B_{z\\epsilon_{1}}n\\varepsilon/3}\\right).\\\\ \\end{split}$ (20)"},{"child_ids":["A1.SS1.p6.1","A1.SS1.p6.1.1","A1.EGx48","A1.E18","A1.SS1.p6.2","A1.SS1.p6.2.1","A1.EGx49","A1.E19","A1.SS1.p6.3","A1.SS1.p6.3.1","A1.EGx50","A1.E20"],"classes":["ltx_para","ltx_noindent"],"id":"A1.SS1.p6","tag":"div","text":"By Lemma A.1 , we have: $\\displaystyle\\begin{split}\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\frac{\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}}{n}-\\boldsymbol{Q}_{zz}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\middle|\\mathcal{A}\\right\\}&=\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\boldsymbol{z}_{i}\\boldsymbol{z}_{i}^{\\top}}{n}-\\boldsymbol{Q}_{zz}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\middle|\\mathcal{A}\\right\\}\\\\ &=\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\sum_{i=1}^{n}(\\boldsymbol{z}_{i}\\boldsymbol{z}_{i}^{\\top}-\\boldsymbol{Q}_{zz})\\right\\|\\geq n\\varepsilon\\middle|\\mathcal{A}\\right\\}\\\\ &\\leq 2q\\exp\\left(-\\frac{n^{2}\\varepsilon^{2}/2}{\\nu(\\bar{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{zz}|\\mathcal{A})+\\bar{B}_{zz}n\\varepsilon/3}\\right).\\end{split}$ (18) Similarly, $\\displaystyle\\begin{split}\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\frac{\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{X}}{n}-\\boldsymbol{Q}_{zx}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\middle|\\mathcal{A}\\right\\}&=\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\boldsymbol{z}_{i}\\boldsymbol{x}_{i}^{\\top}}{n}-\\boldsymbol{Q}_{zx}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\middle|\\mathcal{A}\\right\\}\\\\ &=\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\sum_{i=1}^{n}(\\boldsymbol{z}_{i}\\boldsymbol{x}_{i}^{\\top}-\\boldsymbol{Q}_{zx})\\right\\|\\geq n\\varepsilon\\middle|\\mathcal{A}\\right\\}\\\\ &\\leq(p+q)\\exp\\left(-\\frac{n^{2}\\varepsilon^{2}/2}{\\nu(\\bar{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{zx}|\\mathcal{A})+\\bar{B}_{zx}n\\varepsilon/3}\\right).\\end{split}$ (19) By Assumption 1 (iii), the instrument $\\boldsymbol{z}$ is uncorrelated with the error term $\\epsilon_{1}$ , which implies $\\mathbb{E}[\\boldsymbol{z}\\epsilon_{1}|\\mathcal{A}]=\\boldsymbol{0}$ . Applying Lemma A.1 again, we have: $\\displaystyle\\begin{split}\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\frac{\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{\\mathcal{E}}_{1}}{n}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\middle|\\mathcal{A}\\right\\}&=\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\boldsymbol{z}_{i}{\\epsilon}_{1,i}}{n}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\middle|\\mathcal{A}\\right\\}\\\\ &=\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\boldsymbol{z}_{i}{\\epsilon}_{1,i}\\right\\|\\geq n\\varepsilon\\middle|\\mathcal{A}\\right\\}\\\\ &\\leq(q+1)\\exp\\left(-\\frac{n^{2}\\varepsilon^{2}/2}{\\nu(\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{z\\epsilon_{1}}|\\mathcal{A})+B_{z\\epsilon_{1}}n\\varepsilon/3}\\right).\\\\ \\end{split}$ (20)"},{"child_ids":["A1.E21"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx51","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle\\begin{split}\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|n(\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z})^{-1}-\\boldsymbol{Q}_{ZZ}^{-1}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\middle|\\mathcal{A}\\right\\}&\\leq 2q\\exp\\left(-\\frac{n^{2}(\\lambda_{z}^{2}\\varepsilon)^{2}/2}{\\nu(\\bar{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{zz}|\\mathcal{A})+\\bar{B}_{zz}n(\\lambda_{z}^{2}\\varepsilon)/3}\\right)\\\\ &=2q\\exp\\left(-\\frac{\\lambda_{z}^{4}n^{2}\\varepsilon^{2}/2}{\\nu(\\bar{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{zz}|\\mathcal{A})+\\lambda_{z}^{2}\\bar{B}_{zz}n\\varepsilon/3}\\right).\\end{split}$ (21)"},{"child_ids":["A1.SS1.p7.1","A1.SS1.p7.1.1","A1.EGx51","A1.E21"],"classes":["ltx_para","ltx_noindent"],"id":"A1.SS1.p7","tag":"div","text":"With Lemma A.2 and (18 ), we have: $\\displaystyle\\begin{split}\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|n(\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z})^{-1}-\\boldsymbol{Q}_{ZZ}^{-1}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\middle|\\mathcal{A}\\right\\}&\\leq 2q\\exp\\left(-\\frac{n^{2}(\\lambda_{z}^{2}\\varepsilon)^{2}/2}{\\nu(\\bar{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{zz}|\\mathcal{A})+\\bar{B}_{zz}n(\\lambda_{z}^{2}\\varepsilon)/3}\\right)\\\\ &=2q\\exp\\left(-\\frac{\\lambda_{z}^{4}n^{2}\\varepsilon^{2}/2}{\\nu(\\bar{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{zz}|\\mathcal{A})+\\lambda_{z}^{2}\\bar{B}_{zz}n\\varepsilon/3}\\right).\\end{split}$ (21)"},{"child_ids":["A1.E22"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx52","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle\\begin{split}\\left\\|\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\Theta}}\\right\\|&=\\left\\|\\left(\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}\\right)^{-1}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{X}\\right\\|\\\\ &=\\left\\|\\boldsymbol{\\Theta}+\\left(\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}\\right)^{-1}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{\\mathcal{E}}_{2}\\right\\|\\\\ &\\leq B_{\\Theta}+\\left\\|\\left(\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}\\right)^{-1}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{\\mathcal{E}}_{2}\\right\\|\\\\ &\\leq B_{\\Theta}+\\frac{\\delta_{z\\epsilon_{2}}}{\\lambda_{z}}:=B_{\\hat{\\Theta}}.\\end{split}$ (22)"},{"child_ids":["A1.E23"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx53","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle\\begin{split}\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\frac{1}{n}\\boldsymbol{X}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}(\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z})^{-1}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{\\mathcal{E}}_{1}-\\boldsymbol{0}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\middle|\\mathcal{A}\\right\\}&\\leq(q+1)\\exp\\left(-\\frac{n^{2}(\\frac{\\varepsilon}{B_{\\hat{\\Theta}}})^{2}/2}{\\nu(\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{z\\epsilon_{1}}|\\mathcal{A})+B_{z\\epsilon_{1}}n(\\frac{\\varepsilon}{B_{\\hat{\\Theta}}})/3}\\right)\\\\ &=(q+1)\\exp\\left(-\\frac{n^{2}\\varepsilon^{2}/2}{B_{\\hat{\\Theta}}^{2}\\nu(\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}_{z\\epsilon_{1}}|\\mathcal{A})+B_{\\hat{\\Theta}}B_{z\\epsilon_{1}}n\\varepsilon/3}\\right).\\end{split}$ (23)"},{"child_ids":["A1.Ex26"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx54","tag":"table","text":"$\\displaystyle\\begin{split}&\\mathbb{P}\\left\\{\\left\\|\\frac{1}{n}\\boldsymbol{X}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z}(\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Z})^{-1}\\boldsymbol{Z}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{X}-\\boldsymbol{Q}_{zx}^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{Q}_{zz}^{-1}\\boldsymbol{Q}_{zx}\\right\\|\\geq\\varepsilon\\middle|\\mathcal{A}\\right\\}\\\\ &\\leq 2(p+q)\\exp\\left(-\\frac{n^{2}(\\frac{\\lambda_{z}\\varepsilon}{3B_{zx}})^{2}/2}{\\nu(\\bar{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{zx}|\\mathcal{A})+\\bar{B}_{zx}n(\\frac{\\lambda_{z}\\varepsilon}{3B_{zx}})/3}\\right)+2q\\exp\\left(-\\frac{\\lambda_{z}^{4}n^{2}(\\frac{\\varepsilon}{3B_{zx}^{2}})^{2}/2}{\\nu(\\bar{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{zz}|\\mathcal{A})+\\lambda_{z}^{2}\\bar{B}_{zz}n(\\frac{\\varepsilon}{3B_{zx}^{2}})/3}\\right)\\\\ &=2(p+q)\\exp\\left(-\\frac{\\lambda_{z}^{2}n^{2}\\varepsilon^{2}/2}{9B_{zx}^{2}\\nu(\\bar{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{zx}|\\mathcal{A})+\\lambda_{z}B_{zx}\\bar{B}_{zx}n\\varepsilon}\\right)+2q\\exp\\left(-\\frac{\\lambda_{z}^{4}n^{2}\\varepsilon^{2}/2}{9B_{zx}^{4}\\nu(\\bar{\\boldsymbol{\\Omega}}_{zz}|\\mathcal{A})+\\lambda_{z}^{2}B_{zx}^{2}\\bar{B}_{zz}n\\varepsilon}\\right).\\end{split}$"},{"child_ids":["A1.E24"],"classes":["ltx_equationgroup","ltx_eqn_align","ltx_eqn_table"],"id":"A1.EGx55",